# Round callstream (S1 callpool + S2 callstream), the landing A/B on plan (b′), both cards (the two-card table:
# never beside the A6000 rows): a prompt call that streams its hottest host experts into the residency's churn pool
# (BLOOMERY_HOSTSTREAM=on) against the same binary and residency with streaming off, one lease. Flow model (the
# round's re-derivation on the R3 tip, CED on, G 2, the pool 1,148 experts / 19.26 GB, fill priced at the staging
# thread, 16.77 MB / 1.50 ms): the threshold pick moves the prose P = 4096 wall from 370.3 to 419.7 tok/s, +13.4 %;
# the balance oracle +17.2 % [derived]; the band is the rule's gain widened by the model's misses (5 points each
# side) [derived]. P = 512 (+29.2 % rule, +30.5 % oracle [derived]) is read beside against +22..+32. Decode after
# the call (the -n 96 rows) is read beside against 0..+25 %, the same derivation as callstream-pp-a.card.
kind: ab
question: does streaming the call's hottest host experts into the residency pool raise plan (b′)'s prose prompt
  rate by the flow model's threshold-pick gain, with the decode after the call no slower?
term: pp tok/s @ P = 4096, prose prompt (corpus-prose.ids, the first 4096), no hot list, BLOOMERY_RESIDENCY=
  mid-p40-s1, A6000+3090 (the 3090 at its 250 W cap), plan (b′), CED on, G 2 - (on - off) / off, paired by round
unit: %
predict: +8..+19
rounds: 2
sd: 1.1 % rig-log 09-25#v41-prefill-s14, two binaries' per-round pp ratios, one run's SD about 0.55 and 1.1 %; the
  larger
condition: the callstream tree's generate_ds41, both arms in one lease through the load-time lever, from
  /Users/hckim/repo/bloomery-callstream2 (main d3d54385 + callstream): BLOOMERY_REMOTE='~/repo/bloomery-callstream2' BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=2
  BLOOMERY_DECODE_N=96 BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_GEN_PLACE=bp BLOOMERY_TIMING_CARDS=a6000+3090
  BLOOMERY_RESIDENCY=mid-p40-s1 BLOOMERY_STEP_STATS=1 BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/callstream-pp-bp.card' just
  depth-gpu-ds41 prose:512 prose:4096 prose:512@BLOOMERY_HOSTSTREAM=on prose:4096@BLOOMERY_HOSTSTREAM=on. Two load
  keys a round, each arm from Session::clear; every on row carries `call stream end` with admitted > 0 and kept 1,
  every off row none; the witness blocks show no Xid before or after; no row carries [cold], [cpu-busy] or
  [other-busy]. Box time 10..15 min [derived: 4 loads and one warm-up at 60..110 s (a two-card load, not measured
  by this round), 2 rounds of 4 prompts and 4 decodes of 96]
decide-in: land S2 with streaming off by default and propose on as the default under a residency, both tables and
  the decode rows beside
decide-below: read the on rows' call stream records: backlog_us near pick_us means the staging thread paces the
  call; otherwise the tier's share of the host union left less for the pool to take than the model's bp term -
  re-derive bp's union with the tier rows before any default change
decide-above: the host union shrank past the rule's share: re-fit the flow model's union law on the on rows'
  union_ms and move the floor down (STREAM_FLOOR 16)
